women's health research at Yale has a  training program that's called building  interdisciplinary research careers in  women's health and the focus of this  program is to train the next generation  of researchers on how to conduct team  science in order to increase their  capacity to move forward in their  research careers and to engage in team  science so women's health research at  Yale is really a national leader in  being able to train these junior  investigators in how to conduct research  that takes a more expansive focus then  their careers have taken previously so  it kind of takes them out of their  comfort zone and trains them on how to  engage researchers and other disciplines  to be able to start to collaborate to  put together teams of scientists to  address questions that they're  interested in pursuing  women's health research iel has provided  me as a junior faculty member with a  community of scholars and kindred  spirits so to speak so it's really  provided me with support not only  specific to my research in terms of  mentorship and expertise during the  perinatal period in psychiatry but it's  also provided a community of colleagues  where I can ask questions about career  development and also find support in  general around this area of work the  importance of women's health research  so your research needs to have real  world significance that you need to be  able to identify the work you do and how  it's ultimately going to be related to  the treatment of disease and this has  had a large impact on how i mentor  trainees in my own laboratory now how I  help them consider long-range plans for  their own careers and also always always  stress the practical benefit of their  own research  one of the most exciting things about  being a researcher and a teacher at a  university is that you get to introduce  young people to research and I've had  the good fortune of supervising dozens  of PhD students in my laboratory many of  them over half of them were women and  and it's particularly I think exciting  to those women to be able not only to  learn about this new field of biomedical  engineering and how one might use it in  in health but to think about how it can  be used to improve the health of women  we are only at the beginning of what we  need to know about women's health and  gender differences and so it's clear to  us that we need to train a next  generation of researchers will focus on  the area of women's health and we are so  pleased to have young scientists come to  us to study as junior faculty is  postdoctoral students as undergraduates  and we have many people interested in  doing that and its really been our great  pleasure to integrate them into our  program  you
 

